;; si's AOT's divergences (doc/scheme/SCHEME-SURVEY.md, "As built: SM7 (write-ahead)"): the classes of the non-pass
;; items of bin/si check --aot that the interpreted check does not have (those fall in test/scheme/divergences.edn's,
;; tried after these): a program the AOT refuses ("refused ID: WHY") or a compiled run that differs from si's. An
;; item's class is the first whose :match finds it. Goi's format (test/goi/divergences.edn). Read with the Clojure
;; reader.
[
 {:id :syntax-constants
  :title "syntax objects among a program's constants"
  :kind :deferred
  :why "psyntax leaves syntax objects (its stx and rib records, their marks and labels) in the core forms of a program that uses syntax at run time (#'x outside a transformer); the AOT writes constants as text read back at start, and a record with psyntax's own record types and labels does not read back: the program is refused (SC90)"
  :decided "SC90"
  :match [#"^refused [^ ]+: the compiler refuses it: refused: a constant that does not read back: #\[rtd:stx"]}
]
